ires more CPU, memory or I/O to deliver the same level of service, which increases energy consumption. Proper indexing, good data modelling and regular maintenance help reduce unnecessary resource usage."},{"v":"🤔 To Evaluate"},{"v":"The criterion is validated if a strategy is applied to optimise the database\u2019s performance."},{"v":"Significant"},null,{"v":0.0,"f":"0"},{"v":1.5,"f":"1,5"},{"v":0.0,"f":"0"},null,{"v":null}]},{"c":[null,{"v":"Date(2025,2,4)","f":"4.3"},{"v":"Does the product use the right database/storage technologies for the right usages ?"},{"v":"If the product storage needs are large, it may be beneficial to specialize the storage technologies : \n- PG/MYSQL/Oracle/SQLServer or object relation\n- MongoDB for document oriented.\n- Columnar db for analytics.\n- Specialized database (vector, times series)."},null,{"v":"An improvement potential exists if the project does not use elasticity tools and the load is not constant.\n the projects has some specific storage needs that would be better saved by another storage system, and the volume is significant (\u003e hundreds of go)."},{"v":"Significant"},null,{"v":0.0,"f":"0"},{"v":1.5,"f":"1,5"},{"v":0.0,"f":"0"},null,{"v":null}]},{"c":[null,{"v":"Date(2025,3,4)","f":"4.4"},{"v":"Are the tests databases as big as the production ones ?"},{"v":"Usually it\u0027s not necessary to have as much data in tests environnements than in production."},null,{"v":"An improvement potential exists if some tests databases are as big as the production ones."},{"v":"Significant"},null,{"v":0.0,"f":"0"},{"v":1.5,"f":"1,5"},{"v":0.0,"f":"0"},null,{"v":null}]},{"c":[null,{"v":"Date(2025,4,4)","f":"4.5"},{"v":"Is there data duplications ?"},{"v":"If data is duplicated and this is not part of product strategy as High Availability, this usually indicates an optimisation opportunity, except when the duplication results from intentional performance-driven denormalisation."},null,{"v":"The criterion is validated if the team has i